  "hypotheses_set": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "target": ["e_movie"],
      "entities": [
        { "id": "e_movie", "type": "Movie" },
        { "id": "e_actor", "type": "Person" },
        { "id": "e_streep", "type": "Person" }
      ],
      "relationships": [
        { "id": "r_act", "role": "actor", "from": "e_actor", "to": "e_movie" },
        { "id": "r_streep_movies", "role": "actor", "from": "e_streep", "to": "e_movie" }
      ],
      "constraint": {
        "and_conditions": [
          {
            "or_conditions": [
              {
                "left": { "attribute_name": "name", "of": "e_actor" },
                "operator": "!=",
                "right": "Meryl Streep"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "not_exists": {
              "id": "r_streep_movies",
              "from": "e_actor",
              "to": "e_movie"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

In this query, we are looking for movies (`e_movie`) that have actors (`e_actor`) who are not Meryl Streep (`e_streep`). We also check that there is no relationship between the movie and Meryl Streep in the `r_streep_movies` role. The `not_exists` constraint checks for the absence of a relationship.

 To find movies that have no actors who have worked with Meryl Streep in any movie, we can use a query similar to the one for finding movies directed by Eastwood or Spielberg and starring Meryl Streep, but with an additional condition to check if there are no such actors. Here's the JSON representation of the query:

```json
{
  "hypotheses_set": [
    [
      {
        "id": "q1",
        "target": ["e_movie"],
        "entities": [
          { "id": "e_movie", "type": "Movie" },
          { "id": "e_actor", "type": "Person" },
          { "id": "e_streep", "type": "Person" },
          { "id": "e_actor_streep", "type": "Actor_Movie" }
        ],
        "relationships": [
          { "id": "r_act", "role": "actor", "from": "e_actor", "to": "e_movie" },
          { "id": "r_streep_movies", "role": "starred", "from": "e_streep", "to": "e_actor" }
        ],
        "constraint": {
          "and_conditions": [
            {
              "left": { "attribute_name": "name", "of": "e_streep" },
              "operator": "=",
              "right": "Meryl Streep"
            },
            {
              "or_conditions": [
                {
                  "not_exists": { "id": "r_actor_streep", "in": ["e_actor", "e_movie"] }
                },
                {
                  "left": { "count_id": "r_actor_streep" },
                  "operator": "<",
                  "right": 1
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

In this query, we are checking for movies (`e_movie`) that have actors (`e_actor`) who have not worked with Meryl Streep (`e_streep`). We create an intermediate relationship `r_streep_movies` to represent the fact that a person (`e_streep`) has starred in a movie (`e_movie`).

The condition checks if there is no such relationship between `e_actor` and `e_movie` (`not_exists`) or if the count of such relationships is less than 1.
